  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q17-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "17",
    "prompt": "A bag contains balls numbered 1 through to $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q17-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Two balls are drawn from the bag with replacement and the sum of the numbers is recorded. Find the expected value.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n+1$",
          "worked": "Let $A$ and $B$ be the two numbers drawn. Each ordered pair has probability $\\frac{1}{n^2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(A+B)&=\\frac{1}{n^2}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sum_{j=1}^{n}(i+j)\\\\E(A+B)&=\\frac{2n}{n^2}\\left(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right)\\\\E(A+B)&=n+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q17-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Two balls are drawn from the bag without replacement and the sum of the numbers is recorded. Find the expected value.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$n+1$",
          "worked": "Each ordered pair of distinct numbers has probability $\\frac{1}{[n(n-1)]}$. Each number occurs $n-1$ times in each position.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(A+B)&=\\frac{1}{n(n-1)}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\sum_{\\substack{j=1\\\\j\\ne i}}^{n}(i+j)\\\\E(A+B)&=\\frac{2(n-1)}{n(n-1)}\\left(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right)\\\\E(A+B)&=n+1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q17-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Two balls are drawn from the bag with replacement and the difference between the greatest and least of these numbers is recorded. Find the expected value.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p33-q17-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{1}{3}\\left(n-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p33-q17-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Weight each difference by its probability; a positive difference ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " occurs in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2(n-k)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " ordered pairs.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $D=|A-B|$. For $k=1,\\ldots,n-1$, there are $2(n-k)$ ordered pairs with difference $k$, so $P(D=k)=\\frac{2(n-k)}{n^2}$. The difference $0$ contributes nothing to the expected value.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(D)&=\\frac{2}{n^2}\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}k(n-k)\\\\E(D)&=\\frac{2}{n^2}\\left(n\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}k-\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}k^2\\right)\\\\E(D)&=\\frac{2}{n^2}\\left(\\frac{n^2(n-1)}{2}-\\frac{n(n-1)(2n-1)}{6}\\right)\\\\E(D)&=\\frac{n^2-1}{3n}\\\\E(D)&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(n-\\frac{1}{n}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q17-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Two balls are drawn from the bag without replacement and the difference between the greatest and least of these numbers is recorded. Find the expected value.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p33-q17-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac{n+1}{3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p33-q17-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Count the ordered pairs for each difference and weight by their probabilities.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "There are $n(n-1)$ equally likely ordered pairs. For $k=1,\\ldots,n-1$, exactly $2(n-k)$ have difference $k$.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(D)&=\\frac{2}{n(n-1)}\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1}k(n-k)\\\\E(D)&=\\frac{2}{n(n-1)}\\left(\\frac{n(n-1)(n+1)}{6}\\right)\\\\E(D)&=\\frac{n+1}{3}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      }
    ]
  },
